To calculate the number of Dressers visible in the scene, we can use the Pixel_Depth_Tool to estimate the pixel-level depth from the image. This will help us determine the area where the Dressers are located and, by extension, the number of Dressers. Here's the Python code to achieve this:

```python
import Pixel_Depth_Tool  # Import the Pixel_Depth_Tool

# Execute the function to detect Dressers and estimate depth
depth_instructions = Pixel_Depth_Tool.execute(image=image_path, output=True)
depth_images = depth_instructions['depth_image']
num_dressers = len(depth_images)

print(f"The scene contains {num_dressers} Dressers.")
```

Replace "image_path" with the actual path of the image file you want to use (in this case, "5756_0.png"). The variable `depth_instructions` will contain the result of the `execute` function, and `depth_images` will contain the depth images. The variable `num_dressers` will be set to the actual number of Dressers detected in the image.

When this code is run, it will output the number of Dressers visible in the scene.
